    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d669-a5">

                <pb facs="0900" n="830" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg830"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-12-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 3, 1861.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> It was with a real pleasure that I learned
                    your appointment as envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the
                    United States in China.</p>
                <p>The friendly intercourse of all our predecessors made me always desire the
                    presence of a representative of your government in Peking, and I therefore look
                    forward with impatience to prove once more towards your excellency those
                    sentiments of sincere friendship which have always existed between our
                    respective governments. I am very sorry to state that the advanced season will
                    not permit a personal acquaintance with you before the beginning of the spring,
                    but let me assure you that I shall be most happy to be in anything useful to the
                    success <pb facs="0901" n="831" xml:id="pg831"/> of your mission, and avail
                    myself of this occasion to pray your excellency to agree the high consideration,
                    sir, of your most obedient servant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>L. D. BALLUZEEH.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Burlingame,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary of
                            the United States to China, &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
